# Register New Files in CMakeLists

When adding or moving any engine/game source, update the matching `CMakeLists.txt` in the **same change**. Skipping this leaves the file out of the CMake target, so IntelliSense/clangd report errors and the build ignores the file.

## Checklist (do every time)

1. Add every new `.cpp` to the correct target source list.
2. If you add a new **public** `include/` directory, add it to `target_include_directories(... PUBLIC ...)`.
3. If you add a new `src/module/` tree (or need `"module/Foo.hpp"` includes), ensure the parent `src/` is on `target_include_directories(... PRIVATE ...)` (Renderer already has `Renderer/src`).
4. Do not rely on globbing — list sources explicitly (project convention).

## Where to register

| New file location | Update |
|---|---|
| `Engine/**/src/*.cpp` | `Engine/CMakeLists.txt` → `add_library(SatEngine STATIC ...)` |
| `Engine/**/src/module/*.cpp` | Same — list explicitly (e.g. `Renderer/src/module/MeshPass.cpp`) |
| `Engine/**/include/` (new public dir) | `Engine/CMakeLists.txt` → `target_include_directories(SatEngine PUBLIC ...)` |
| `Engine/**/src/` (for `module/` includes) | `target_include_directories(SatEngine PRIVATE ...)` — not PUBLIC |
| `GamePlayer/src/*.cpp` | `GamePlayer/CMakeLists.txt` → `add_executable(GamePlayer ...)` |

## Example

```cmake
# After creating Engine/Renderer/src/module/MeshPass.cpp — also edit Engine/CMakeLists.txt:
add_library(SatEngine STATIC
    # ... existing sources ...
    Renderer/src/module/MeshPass.cpp
)

# Private so "module/MeshPass.hpp" resolves without exposing internals publicly:
target_include_directories(SatEngine PRIVATE
    "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/Renderer/src"
)
```

Public headers under an already-registered `include/` path do not need a CMake entry. Module headers under `src/module/` are private; only their `.cpp` files and the private `src/` include path need CMake updates.
